\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Gracious Spirit, Holy Ghost, 
\par Taught by Thee, we covet most,
\par Of Thy gifts at Pentecost,
\par Holy, heavenly love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Faith that mountains could remove,
\par Tongues of earth or heaven above,
\par Knowledge, all things, empty prove
\par Without heavenly love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Through I as a martyr bleed,
\par Give my goods the poor to feed,
\par All is vain if love I need;
\par Therefore give me love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Love is kind, and suffers long,
\par Love is meek, and thinks no wrong,
\par Love than death itself more strong
\par Therefore give us love,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Prophecy will fade away,
\par Melting in the light of day;
\par Love will ever with us stay:
\par Therefore give us love
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Faith, and hope, and love we see,
\par Joining hand in hand, agree;
\par But the greatest of the three,
\par And the best, is love,
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

